.TH bhtune-template 1  "bhtune-template " 
.SH NAME
bhtune\-template \- Inspect and manage DCS/PLC templates
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-template\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect and manage DCS/PLC templates
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bhtune\-template\-list(1)
List every template (built\-in and user\-imported)
.TP
bhtune\-template\-show(1)
Show one template\*(Aqs full detail as JSON
.TP
bhtune\-template\-import(1)
Import a template from a file. Accepts either a single template as JSON (see `template export`\*(Aqs default output shape) or a multi\-template TOML catalog (the same `[[template]]` array\-of\-tables shape as the embedded/user catalog, see `template export \-\-format toml`) \-\- the format is auto\-detected from the file\*(Aqs content, not its extension. A JSON single\-template import is rejected outright if a template with that name already exists; a TOML catalog import instead skips (and reports) any template whose name already exists, so re\-importing an updated community catalog only adds what\*(Aqs new
.TP
bhtune\-template\-export(1)
Export a template to a file, e.g. as a starting point for a site\-specific copy or a community catalog contribution
.TP
bhtune\-template\-delete(1)
Delete a template. Refuses if any saved loop still references it. A `Builtin`\- or `Catalog`\-origin template reappears automatically the next time bhtune starts unless it\*(Aqs also removed from its source (bhtune\-core\*(Aqs embedded catalog for `Builtin`, which only a new bhtune release can change; the user catalog file for `Catalog`)
.TP
bhtune\-template\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
